WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.063 --> 00:01.963
(Supported by KOCCA)

3
00:02.033 --> 00:03.332
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds are fictitious.)

4
00:03.333 --> 00:04.633
(Children were filmed under production guidelines.)

5
00:05.633 --> 00:07.103
Where did you get this?

6
00:07.173 --> 00:08.203
Give it back right now.

7
00:09.203 --> 00:10.203
If you tell me how an unpublished book...

8
00:10.273 --> 00:12.913
- ended up here. - Hurry up and give it to me.

9
00:12.973 --> 00:15.243
Give it back. I said give it to me.

10
00:15.313 --> 00:16.883
Hand it over right now.

11
00:31.023 --> 00:32.023
I am sorry.

12
00:39.903 --> 00:41.203
I apologize.

13
00:41.233 --> 00:43.373
It is a very important book to me, so I acted on instinct.

14
00:44.543 --> 00:45.643
It is mine.

15
00:46.913 --> 00:50.313
Where did you get that? It is not even published yet.

16
00:51.483 --> 00:53.783
Well, do I have to tell you that?

17
00:55.723 --> 00:59.253
I saved you, and I ate a moth for you.

18
00:59.353 --> 01:01.353
Is it really that hard to tell me one thing?

19
01:03.623 --> 01:04.623
I do not know.

20
01:04.693 --> 01:06.663
I just happened to get my hands on it.

21
01:06.733 --> 01:07.833
I swear...

22
01:10.863 --> 01:12.533
I mean, I...

23
01:13.173 --> 01:15.333
I have been waiting for that book for a really long time.

24
01:15.403 --> 01:16.573
Did something happen to the author?

25
01:16.643 --> 01:18.443
I read volumes one and two over and over,

26
01:18.503 --> 01:20.343
worrying if Byeol I and Moon Bear were doing well.

27
01:20.413 --> 01:21.613
I have waited for years.

28
01:27.683 --> 01:29.583
So please tell me.

29
01:30.653 --> 01:31.753
Where did you get it?

30
01:35.423 --> 01:37.063
I do not remember.

31
01:37.963 --> 01:40.793
Seriously. Then can you lend it to me?

32
01:41.763 --> 01:43.233
I will read it quickly and give it back.

33
01:43.733 --> 01:45.933
No. I said no.

34
01:46.003 --> 01:48.903
It is because I really need it right now.

35
01:51.943 --> 01:53.073
Come in.

36
01:53.913 --> 01:55.513
I am asking you so politely,

37
01:55.583 --> 01:57.313
can you not at least pretend to listen?

38
01:59.053 --> 02:00.513
Are you okay?

39
02:00.983 --> 02:02.483
Everyone is waiting outside.

40
02:06.723 --> 02:09.363
(Ryu Min)

41
02:10.923 --> 02:11.963
Min.

42
02:12.733 --> 02:13.962
Give her an autograph.

43
02:13.963 --> 02:14.963
What?

44
02:15.433 --> 02:16.933
She says she is a fan.

45
02:17.363 --> 02:19.703
We will talk about the book after filming.

46
02:20.273 --> 02:22.603
I have nothing more to say.

47
02:22.673 --> 02:23.703
Hey, well...

48
02:24.703 --> 02:26.473
(Ryu Min)

49
02:33.413 --> 02:34.883
Where should I...

50
02:35.013 --> 02:36.153
Excuse me?

51
02:36.823 --> 02:37.853
My autograph.

52
02:41.053 --> 02:42.423
I told you not to come see me anymore.

53
02:42.493 --> 02:44.023
I do not want you to see me like this.

54
02:45.193 --> 02:48.033
I want that too.

55
02:48.133 --> 02:49.403
But...

56
02:49.463 --> 02:51.803
what can I do when my feet keep bringing me here?

57
02:51.963 --> 02:54.903
Cut, okay. Hey, the emotion was great.

58
02:54.933 --> 02:56.303
Let us shoot the reverse.

59
02:56.403 --> 02:58.543
What is this, the moth effect or what?

60
02:58.603 --> 03:00.573
How is everything getting an okay in one take?

61
03:00.813 --> 03:03.813
Hey, let us shoot this quickly without any bloopers, okay?

62
03:03.883 --> 03:05.613
- Okay. - Okay.

63
03:05.683 --> 03:08.253
- Hey. - Yes. Mouthwash?

64
03:11.653 --> 03:13.453
- Producer. - Yes?

65
03:13.593 --> 03:16.823
By any chance, is your friend already asleep?

66
03:17.893 --> 03:19.633
I am not sure.

67
03:19.733 --> 03:20.863
But...

68
03:20.933 --> 03:23.533
before the female lead goes into the room,

69
03:23.603 --> 03:26.133
he is supposed to come meet her.

70
03:26.173 --> 03:28.433
Then shouldn't the lights be off?

71
03:31.573 --> 03:33.143
- Right, yes. - Yes.

72
03:34.673 --> 03:35.843
("Byeol I and Moon Bear")

73
03:46.553 --> 03:49.163
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 3)

74
03:59.103 --> 04:00.103
Bear.

75
04:01.133 --> 04:04.073
Even though bamboo is so thin and tall,

76
04:04.143 --> 04:06.813
the reason it does not break in a typhoon...

77
04:06.873 --> 04:10.913
is because it is empty inside and has joints.

78
04:10.983 --> 04:13.583
People have joints too,

79
04:13.653 --> 04:16.523
and when they despair, hurt,

80
04:16.583 --> 04:20.953
part ways, and fail, they say one forms each time.

81
04:21.593 --> 04:22.593
(Nodding)

82
04:22.723 --> 04:23.923
You are the same, right?

83
04:25.023 --> 04:26.793
For the things people did wrong,

84
04:28.193 --> 04:30.263
I will apologize on their behalf.

85
04:31.833 --> 04:33.673
How could they do that?

86
04:34.933 --> 04:36.343
Just for their own greed,

87
04:37.343 --> 04:39.773
how could they do that to their family?

88
04:42.543 --> 04:45.753
Mom, why did you skip a meal again?

89
04:49.623 --> 04:51.653
("Polyamory")

90
04:52.653 --> 04:53.723
What is this now?

91
04:55.693 --> 04:56.723
Your dad said...

92
04:57.923 --> 05:00.933
I might understand him better if I read it.

93
05:06.233 --> 05:07.373
Where is he?

94
05:09.343 --> 05:10.703
He should be in your room.

95
05:14.943 --> 05:16.343
What are you doing? Get out.

96
05:20.413 --> 05:22.253
What is this?

97
05:22.313 --> 05:25.553
- I told you not to write about us. - Why not?

98
05:25.623 --> 05:28.353
Why not? You said it yourself.

99
05:28.423 --> 05:31.123
Everything a writer experiences is firewood.

100
05:31.223 --> 05:33.163
You told me to burn it deep and keep burning it.

101
05:35.703 --> 05:38.663
Do not melt your personal feelings into your writing.

102
05:38.703 --> 05:40.203
Making money through writing is not easy.

103
05:40.273 --> 05:42.703
I know it is hard to make money just by looking at you.

104
05:42.773 --> 05:46.143
Family, loyalty, love, duty, affection,

105
05:46.213 --> 05:47.973
pulling out things you do not feel to write about them,

106
05:48.043 --> 05:49.213
you must have suffered so much.

107
05:50.313 --> 05:51.643
(Gong Yu Il)

108
05:52.043 --> 05:53.053
College.

109
05:54.083 --> 05:55.783
You got into such a good one, so why go there?

110
05:55.853 --> 05:57.223
They offered me a scholarship.

111
05:57.283 --> 05:58.623
Hey, if it is about money, I will...

112
05:58.683 --> 06:00.423
I do not need it anymore.

113
06:00.493 --> 06:03.463
Because I will not accept any help from you.

114
06:14.233 --> 06:15.573
Cut, okay.

115
06:16.703 --> 06:17.703
Great work, everyone.

116
06:17.773 --> 06:20.013
- Great work. - Great work, Director.

117
06:20.073 --> 06:21.813
- Great work. - Great work.

118
06:21.873 --> 06:24.213
Yes, head back. Good job.

119
06:25.643 --> 06:27.313
Did she fall asleep already?

120
06:28.413 --> 06:29.453
Whatever.

121
06:29.523 --> 06:31.383
Does she think I cannot find it without her?

122
06:31.453 --> 06:33.993
I do not think you can find it. You have not found it for years,

123
06:34.053 --> 06:35.493
so how will you find it now?

124
06:35.553 --> 06:37.963
Instead of hitting me with facts,

125
06:38.023 --> 06:41.363
- give me some hope or something. - But...

126
06:41.463 --> 06:43.563
My mouth feels dry, so how about a glass of beer?

127
06:43.633 --> 06:44.903
Forget it.

128
06:44.963 --> 06:46.533
I knew I'd get rejected.

129
06:46.603 --> 06:47.873
I'll let it slide since you're handsome.

130
06:49.033 --> 06:53.043
Oh, my, who is this? I'm finally seeing you.

131
06:53.113 --> 06:55.513
My daughter told me you were filming a movie here.

132
06:55.573 --> 06:58.983
- Oh, my, I wondered if it was true. - Yes, it's true.

133
06:59.043 --> 07:02.283
Could I get a handshake?

134
07:02.353 --> 07:03.353
Sure.

135
07:05.123 --> 07:06.923
I'll definitely watch the live broadcast.

136
07:06.993 --> 07:10.193
- I'll go see the movie too. - Yes, thank you.

137
07:10.263 --> 07:13.033
- Let me take a picture too. - Ma'am, about the picture...

138
07:13.093 --> 07:14.233
No, it's fine.

139
07:16.203 --> 07:18.433
- How long have you been waiting? - Oh, not that long.

140
07:18.503 --> 07:20.273
I only waited three hours.

141
07:20.333 --> 07:22.543
I thought my knees were going to kill me.

142
07:22.603 --> 07:24.643
But seeing your face cures it all.

143
07:25.703 --> 07:29.213
- Oh, thank you. Good luck. - Yes.

144
07:29.313 --> 07:30.743
- Yes. - Yes, I'll be going.

145
07:30.813 --> 07:32.383
- Yes. - Good luck.

146
07:36.423 --> 07:37.723
We're packing up.

147
07:38.883 --> 07:39.923
We're packing up.

148
07:41.653 --> 07:43.993
Mu I, earlier, when you were saving that woman,

149
07:44.063 --> 07:47.463
you almost got seriously hurt. Don't do that from now on.

150
07:48.063 --> 07:49.063
Okay.

151
07:50.703 --> 07:52.002
- Yeong Su. - Yes.

152
07:52.003 --> 07:53.833
It's a huge relief I didn't get hurt, right?

153
07:54.273 --> 07:56.173
Do you even have to ask?

154
07:56.343 --> 07:58.273
You have movie stage greetings and a bunch of shoots lined up.

155
07:59.743 --> 08:00.873
That's what I'm saying.

156
08:02.443 --> 08:03.683
I'm that busy.

157
08:05.853 --> 08:07.083
So about that,

158
08:07.683 --> 08:09.483
you need to do something for me.

159
08:09.553 --> 08:11.153
What? Do what?

160
08:18.293 --> 08:20.133
I thought you didn't have a shoot.

161
08:20.193 --> 08:23.463
- What brings you here? - It's about that incident.

162
08:24.633 --> 08:27.773
Tak Mu I said he would just let that go.

163
08:27.833 --> 08:31.173
He was going to let it go. But thinking about it,

164
08:31.243 --> 08:33.473
he thought you must have been very shocked that day, Gong Yu Il,

165
08:33.543 --> 08:37.743
so Mu I was worried and sent this.

166
08:37.813 --> 08:39.353
What?

167
08:39.483 --> 08:41.353
He's not the type to do that.

168
08:44.053 --> 08:45.253
Our Mu I,

169
08:45.323 --> 08:47.093
sometimes when he gets fixated on something, he only sees that,

170
08:47.153 --> 08:49.963
so he can be a little late to notice his surroundings.

171
08:52.123 --> 08:54.963
I think you're similar in that regard.

172
08:58.963 --> 08:59.973
The stalker fan.

173
09:01.203 --> 09:03.003
I'm sorry about that.

174
09:09.283 --> 09:12.283
My mistake. Well, since I'm already apologizing,

175
09:13.283 --> 09:16.353
let me apologize for one more thing. By any chance,

176
09:16.453 --> 09:19.053
could you lend me Volume Three of "Byeol I and Moon Bear"?

177
09:19.123 --> 09:20.253
I knew it.

178
09:21.553 --> 09:22.893
Ta-da.

179
09:22.963 --> 09:24.293
(The next day)

180
09:24.363 --> 09:26.333
I wondered if you might have changed your mind overnight,

181
09:26.393 --> 09:27.463
so I came back.

182
09:27.533 --> 09:29.963
Could you lend "Byeol I and Moon Bear"...

183
09:30.033 --> 09:31.233
I'm sorry.

184
09:34.503 --> 09:36.043
(The day after that)

185
09:36.103 --> 09:40.373
I brought some premium beef, so "Byeol I and Moon Bear"...

186
09:40.443 --> 09:44.283
Well, if you don't want to lend it,

187
09:44.343 --> 09:46.353
he told me to ask if you're willing to sell it, so I...

188
09:46.413 --> 09:50.383
- Oh my. - I said no, I'm not selling it.

189
09:50.453 --> 09:52.583
Do I have to sell everything just because he tells me to?

190
09:52.653 --> 09:55.823
I wouldn't sell it even if Tak Mu I's grandfather came.

191
09:55.893 --> 09:58.563
- Absolutely never. - Oh, my.

192
09:58.623 --> 09:59.633
Well...

193
10:16.483 --> 10:18.143
It melts in my mouth, probably because it's premium beef.

194
10:19.853 --> 10:21.483
Does she really hate me?

195
10:22.883 --> 10:24.453
I am Tak Mu I, after all.

196
10:24.523 --> 10:26.993
That is the problem. It is because you are Tak Mu I.

197
10:27.053 --> 10:29.523
You treated an innocent person like a stalker,

198
10:29.593 --> 10:30.963
so I would not give it to you either.

199
10:32.563 --> 10:34.163
You were worse than me!

200
10:35.533 --> 10:38.203
That is because my actor said she was a stalker,

201
10:38.263 --> 10:41.303
so without a single doubt, I accused her.

202
10:41.373 --> 10:43.973
Exactly, so I am dying here.

203
10:44.043 --> 10:45.673
Without a single moment of hesitation,

204
10:45.743 --> 10:48.143
should we go just one more time?

205
10:48.213 --> 10:50.883
If you go one more time,

206
10:50.943 --> 10:53.683
I think I will be reported as a stalker.

207
10:53.753 --> 10:55.013
She even said that even if your grandfather came,

208
10:55.083 --> 10:57.053
she would absolutely never sell it.

209
10:57.523 --> 10:58.923
Then do you want to go with my grandmother?

210
11:00.153 --> 11:02.293
No, let us send Min.

211
11:02.353 --> 11:04.163
She might give up the book since she is a fan of Min.

212
11:05.293 --> 11:06.293
Open wide.

213
11:07.993 --> 11:09.293
You can eat at a time like this?

214
11:13.233 --> 11:14.333
It goes down just fine.

215
11:16.373 --> 11:17.843
Are you not going to eat?

216
11:17.903 --> 11:21.573
Hey. We are getting too close these days.

217
11:21.643 --> 11:22.643
When I moved in here,

218
11:22.713 --> 11:24.183
you only visited once and never came back,

219
11:24.243 --> 11:27.413
but now, you are coming over way too often.

220
11:32.553 --> 11:33.593
An autograph.

221
11:35.993 --> 11:37.823
- Ta-da. - Hey.

222
11:38.463 --> 11:41.663
What is this? Why are you giving this to me now?

223
11:46.973 --> 11:48.133
What are you doing?

224
11:48.673 --> 11:50.903
If I die like this, engrave it on my tombstone.

225
11:50.973 --> 11:52.703
"Died from being too touched."

226
11:54.613 --> 11:56.613
("I Didn't Know Back Then")

227
11:57.613 --> 11:59.313
Hey, what is this?

228
12:00.613 --> 12:02.053
Ta-da.

229
12:02.823 --> 12:04.923
- Are you a flower? - Yes.

230
12:05.053 --> 12:06.623
Gosh, how childish.

231
12:06.693 --> 12:09.993
- Are you not busy? - You were worried, so I wondered.

232
12:10.063 --> 12:11.293
I was too curious to hold back.

233
12:11.363 --> 12:12.663
(Da Hong came instead of flowers.)

234
12:12.723 --> 12:14.963
I even missed the VIP premiere because of the shoot.

235
12:16.433 --> 12:17.463
Hey,

236
12:17.533 --> 12:19.773
you are putting in way too much unnecessary effort.

237
12:22.333 --> 12:27.143
This is my passionate devotion for you.

238
12:27.673 --> 12:28.843
Tteokbokki. Oh, my.

239
12:30.783 --> 12:33.583
I just ate earlier.

240
12:34.083 --> 12:35.713
Are you eating again after you already had a meal?

241
12:35.783 --> 12:36.923
I have to.

242
12:40.193 --> 12:41.223
It is delicious.

243
12:42.963 --> 12:44.163
You are so lucky.

244
12:44.223 --> 12:46.333
You do not gain weight even when you eat that much.

245
12:46.363 --> 12:48.293
- Eat some. - I am good.

246
12:50.403 --> 12:52.203
He sleeps so well even with us talking.

247
12:52.833 --> 12:55.533
- Did he not sleep yesterday either? - He could not sleep all night,

248
12:56.243 --> 12:58.173
and it seems he fell asleep for a bit at dawn,

249
12:58.243 --> 13:00.243
so I practically had to carry him out to get here.

250
13:03.243 --> 13:04.443
I feel so bad for him.

251
13:11.683 --> 13:13.153
- What is that? - It is a bear.

252
13:13.223 --> 13:14.823
- It is a bear. - It is a bear.

253
13:14.893 --> 13:17.023
- It is a bear. - Oh, no, it is a bear.

254
13:17.093 --> 13:18.893
- Hold on a second. - Stay back. It is dangerous.

255
13:18.963 --> 13:20.963
- What do we do? - A bear came down.

256
13:21.033 --> 13:23.863
- What? There is a bear in front. - We are trapped.

257
13:23.933 --> 13:26.503
- It is coming. - Shoot it quickly.

258
13:26.573 --> 13:28.533
Shoot it quickly. It is running away!

259
13:45.353 --> 13:47.023
Mu I.

260
13:47.123 --> 13:48.123
Mu I.

261
13:53.963 --> 13:54.993
What is it? Did you have a dream?

262
13:56.303 --> 13:57.303
What?

263
13:58.803 --> 14:01.973
- Yes. - What dream makes you sweat?

264
14:03.343 --> 14:05.273
When interpreting dreams, Ju Da Hong is the best.

265
14:05.343 --> 14:07.973
Tell me. I will see if it is a dream about the movie becoming a huge hit.

266
14:08.073 --> 14:09.613
Yes.

267
14:09.643 --> 14:10.683
Well...

268
14:13.053 --> 14:14.213
Moon Bear...

269
14:14.283 --> 14:15.783
No.

270
14:15.853 --> 14:17.783
- A moon bear... - Yes.

271
14:17.853 --> 14:19.623
It came down to the village to find food.

272
14:21.253 --> 14:23.723
Then it got shot,

273
14:23.793 --> 14:25.023
and blood...

274
14:25.093 --> 14:28.533
The half-moon shape on its chest turned red.

275
14:32.833 --> 14:34.073
And then,

276
14:34.603 --> 14:36.033
it started losing consciousness.

277
14:37.273 --> 14:38.803
- Losing consciousness? - Losing consciousness?

278
14:40.913 --> 14:41.913
But,

279
14:43.883 --> 14:45.013
that was me.

280
14:46.883 --> 14:48.253
What?

281
14:48.313 --> 14:50.323
So it was not just a nonsense dream, it was a bear dream?

282
14:53.693 --> 14:54.693
I get it.

283
14:55.923 --> 14:57.863
You said the Moon Bear was hungry.

284
14:59.933 --> 15:01.433
Mu I, you are hungry right now too, right?

285
15:01.493 --> 15:03.163
That is it.

286
15:03.233 --> 15:04.402
- Eat up. - That's right.

287
15:04.403 --> 15:07.173
A well-fed bear has a shiny coat. Here.

288
15:07.233 --> 15:08.773
- I am fine. - Just one bite.

289
15:08.833 --> 15:10.243
- I am not eating. - Just take one bite.

290
15:10.303 --> 15:11.503
- I said I am not eating! - Just one bite.

291
15:12.873 --> 15:13.873
Hey.

292
15:15.513 --> 15:17.183
- Oh, seriously. - Hey.

293
15:17.243 --> 15:18.243
Sorry.

294
15:20.453 --> 15:22.853
- Enjoy the movie. - I am a big fan.

295
15:24.923 --> 15:25.923
Hello.

296
15:27.493 --> 15:31.063
Oh, why did I have to cover a shift on a day like this?

297
15:31.163 --> 15:33.193
At this point, even I would not believe it.

298
15:34.893 --> 15:36.863
("I Didn't Know Back Then" Premiere)

299
15:36.933 --> 15:40.403
(Theater 1 Exit)

300
15:42.033 --> 15:44.643
He will definitely think I followed him again.

301
15:45.943 --> 15:47.713
("I Didn't Know Back Then" Premiere)

302
15:52.843 --> 15:54.753
The actors will now enter.

303
15:58.553 --> 16:00.553
("I Didn't Know Back Then" Premiere)

304
16:04.023 --> 16:05.063
Go, Tak Mu I!

305
16:07.033 --> 16:08.133
You are so handsome.

306
16:09.763 --> 16:11.333
Let's hit ten million.

307
16:12.863 --> 16:14.003
Go for it.

308
16:15.633 --> 16:16.873
Go for it.

309
16:19.473 --> 16:20.543
("I Didn't Know Back Then," reach ten million viewers!)

310
16:23.483 --> 16:25.143
- Why are you acting like this? - Get out.

311
16:25.213 --> 16:26.513
It is a bear.

312
16:26.583 --> 16:29.753
- Do not move. - A bear is here.

313
16:29.823 --> 16:31.183
A bear.

314
16:31.253 --> 16:32.823
We have to kill the bear!

315
16:37.363 --> 16:40.763
- We have to kill the bear. - Catch it.

316
16:40.833 --> 16:43.103
Hey, what is wrong with you? Are you okay?

317
16:43.163 --> 16:44.733
- Hey, Mu I. - What is it?

318
16:44.803 --> 16:46.433
He is leaving.

319
16:46.503 --> 16:50.173
- What is it? - Hey, why are you... Hey, Mu I.

320
16:54.873 --> 16:58.013
Hey, Mu I. What is wrong with you?

321
16:59.783 --> 17:00.913
What should we do about this?

322
17:01.953 --> 17:04.483
Excuse me, ma'am. Close the door, quickly.

323
17:06.283 --> 17:07.953
- Excuse me, do you have a bag? - What? A bag?

324
17:08.023 --> 17:09.093
A bag.

325
17:13.163 --> 17:14.193
I am sorry.

326
17:15.563 --> 17:17.603
Hey, Mu I, try to breathe.

327
17:17.663 --> 17:20.633
Please try to breathe, please. A bag.

328
17:21.033 --> 17:22.403
A bag, quickly.

329
17:25.673 --> 17:26.843
Breathe.

330
17:32.083 --> 17:33.083
Are you okay?

331
17:52.433 --> 17:53.433
Da Hong.

332
17:54.803 --> 17:55.833
Mu I, are you awake?

333
17:55.903 --> 17:57.903
(Gangseong General Hospital)

334
17:57.973 --> 17:59.243
We are at Jae Gyu's hospital.

335
17:59.303 --> 18:01.343
Yeong Su went back to the office for a bit.

336
18:01.413 --> 18:03.743
They said you suddenly started hyperventilating.

337
18:03.813 --> 18:04.813
Do you remember?

338
18:06.713 --> 18:08.252
What time is it? What about the premiere?

339
18:08.253 --> 18:10.283
Stay lying down.

340
18:10.353 --> 18:11.923
It is already over.

341
18:13.023 --> 18:14.193
It must've been a disaster.

342
18:15.393 --> 18:16.693
Do you want me to show you?

343
18:17.123 --> 18:18.493
For your peace of mind,

344
18:18.563 --> 18:19.963
it would be best if you did not look at it.

345
18:22.763 --> 18:25.163
Never mind. I will just read them to you.

346
18:25.233 --> 18:27.533
Mild or spicy?

347
18:27.633 --> 18:30.303
I will take the mild version, please.

348
18:30.773 --> 18:31.773
Okay.

349
18:32.873 --> 18:35.343
(Tak Mu I Premiere)

350
18:35.413 --> 18:37.613
"I even took a day off to see Tak Mu I,"

351
18:37.683 --> 18:39.183
"but at the public premiere,"

352
18:39.243 --> 18:40.913
"he barely showed his face before leaving."

353
18:40.983 --> 18:42.353
"Tak Mu I from 'I Didn't Know Back Then.'"

354
18:42.413 --> 18:43.983
"I did not know he would be like this."

355
18:44.053 --> 18:45.553
"Power trip by the lead actor?"

356
18:45.623 --> 18:47.953
"Does Tak Mu I look down on moviegoers?"

357
18:48.023 --> 18:49.023
"Tak Mu I's blockbuster,"

358
18:49.093 --> 18:50.693
"audience anticipation ratings plummet."

359
18:50.763 --> 18:51.993
"To blame it on a no-show..."

360
18:52.063 --> 18:53.533
(Gangseong General Hospital)

361
18:53.593 --> 18:55.263
Wait,

362
18:55.333 --> 18:58.503
excuse me, ma'am. I ordered the mild version.

363
18:59.703 --> 19:01.403
This is the mild version.

364
19:01.473 --> 19:04.473
Do you want me to serve up the spicy one instead?

365
19:04.543 --> 19:08.473
Da Hong, sometimes you are truly too cruel.

366
19:11.613 --> 19:12.613
Yes?

367
19:13.753 --> 19:14.913
Are you feeling better?

368
19:16.483 --> 19:19.353
- Yes. - This was delivered for you.

369
19:24.763 --> 19:25.993
Who sent it?

370
19:26.063 --> 19:27.693
A courier dropped it off a little while ago.

371
19:30.833 --> 19:32.063
That I was admitted...

372
19:32.133 --> 19:33.503
No.

373
19:33.573 --> 19:36.303
Is it known that I am at this hospital?

374
19:36.373 --> 19:39.643
No, Dr. Jae Gyu told us to keep it a secret.

375
19:39.703 --> 19:42.643
But the courier seemed to know everything when he arrived.

376
19:44.483 --> 19:45.613
(Why did that happen?)

377
19:45.683 --> 19:47.953
(Are you okay? I'm so worried.)

378
19:51.823 --> 19:52.983
Where are you going?

379
20:12.373 --> 20:14.173
Excuse me, sir!

380
20:17.013 --> 20:18.313
Sir!

381
20:18.383 --> 20:20.083
- Are you okay? - Oh, my.

382
20:20.453 --> 20:22.113
Her phone number?

383
20:22.183 --> 20:24.023
I have no idea.

384
20:24.123 --> 20:26.083
I was just coming out from another delivery,

385
20:26.153 --> 20:28.253
and some woman asked if I was a courier.

386
20:28.323 --> 20:31.463
I said yes, I am, and asked if it was not obvious.

387
20:31.523 --> 20:33.793
Then she just shoved 50 dollars into my hand...

388
20:33.863 --> 20:36.233
and handed me that blue paper bag.

389
20:36.293 --> 20:39.363
For such a short distance, she didn't even ask about the fee...

390
20:39.433 --> 20:41.033
and just gave me 50 dollars,

391
20:41.103 --> 20:43.403
so I did think it was a little strange.

392
20:43.503 --> 20:45.743
By any chance, did that woman...

393
20:45.803 --> 20:47.673
have short hair,

394
20:47.743 --> 20:49.913
a petite build, and pale skin?

395
20:49.983 --> 20:52.913
What? She was quite tall.

396
20:52.983 --> 20:54.883
And I think her hair was really long.

397
20:54.953 --> 20:56.953
Her skin was on the tanner side too.

398
20:57.023 --> 20:59.453
Anyway, she was sexy.

399
20:59.523 --> 21:02.623
She was dripping with sex appeal from head to toe.

400
21:05.263 --> 21:06.893
Hey, you are not even feeling well.

401
21:08.193 --> 21:09.433
Are you okay?

402
21:09.493 --> 21:12.263
What happened? Did you catch them? Who did he say sent it?

403
21:17.303 --> 21:19.773
I already have a million things to worry about.

404
21:22.143 --> 21:24.613
- Darn it, seriously. - Why? Are you okay?

405
21:24.683 --> 21:26.043
- What is it? - Are you okay?

406
21:27.453 --> 21:29.513
(Why did that happen?)

407
21:29.583 --> 21:31.153
(Are you okay? I'm so worried.)

408
21:52.343 --> 21:53.773
Why aren't you answering your phone?

409
21:55.373 --> 21:58.913
- Grandma! - Oh, come here. Oh, my baby.

410
21:58.983 --> 22:00.713
Grandma.

411
22:00.783 --> 22:05.053
- What brings you here so early? - I was on my way to a shoot nearby.

412
22:05.123 --> 22:07.353
- I see. - Get up, you need to eat something.

413
22:08.353 --> 22:09.593
I'm fine.

414
22:10.123 --> 22:12.963
I've been getting so much hate lately,

415
22:13.023 --> 22:14.563
I feel like I'm going to burst.

416
22:14.633 --> 22:16.563
I heard you're starting a new project right away.

417
22:16.963 --> 22:17.963
Good for you.

418
22:18.033 --> 22:19.363
It's better to stay busy at times like this.

419
22:20.533 --> 22:22.033
I think so too.

420
22:22.733 --> 22:25.643
Work on your project, and date too.

421
22:25.703 --> 22:26.973
Are you seeing anyone?

422
22:28.343 --> 22:29.343
No.

423
22:30.613 --> 22:32.643
Don't forget your promise to me.

424
22:32.913 --> 22:34.913
The condition for you to keep acting.

425
22:34.983 --> 22:36.753
Whether it's marriage or dating,

426
22:36.823 --> 22:38.723
you only do it with someone in the same industry.

427
22:40.093 --> 22:41.123
Not this again.

428
22:42.423 --> 22:43.623
Mu I.

429
22:45.393 --> 22:48.433
- Ma'am! - How have you been?

430
22:48.493 --> 22:52.233
Yes. You haven't changed a bit.

431
22:52.363 --> 22:54.433
Oh, you've gotten even prettier.

432
22:55.533 --> 22:56.873
Mu I.

433
22:56.943 --> 22:58.573
If you're going to date anyone, date Da Hong.

434
22:59.773 --> 23:02.043
Why would I date her?

435
23:02.113 --> 23:04.243
Why not? She's bright and lovely.

436
23:04.943 --> 23:07.783
Since you do the same work, you'll understand each other well.

437
23:07.853 --> 23:09.353
Right, Ma'am?

438
23:10.483 --> 23:11.683
What now?

439
23:11.753 --> 23:13.123
How did you get in?

440
23:13.693 --> 23:15.123
I ran into Yeong Su out front.

441
23:15.193 --> 23:17.463
- Oh, you're here? - Yes.

442
23:17.863 --> 23:20.493
Da Hong said she was going to eat with Mu I...

443
23:20.563 --> 23:21.993
and go to the commercial shoot together,

444
23:22.063 --> 23:23.663
so she told me to open the door.

445
23:23.763 --> 23:25.203
And you just let her in?

446
23:25.263 --> 23:26.833
Who can say no to Da Hong?

447
23:26.903 --> 23:28.873
- Oh, man. - Good job.

448
23:28.933 --> 23:30.603
Don't say no to her in the future, either.

449
23:30.673 --> 23:32.573
Never say no to her.

450
23:32.643 --> 23:33.773
You're the best, ma'am.

451
23:35.213 --> 23:36.643
I brought sushi. Let's eat together.

452
23:36.713 --> 23:37.813
Oh, let's do that.

453
23:39.043 --> 23:40.253
I'll go plate it.

454
23:40.313 --> 23:42.813
Because an actress has to eat beautifully, even for one bite.

455
23:42.883 --> 23:43.883
Right.

456
23:47.753 --> 23:50.663
She's bright and lovely. She's so pretty.

457
23:50.723 --> 23:51.993
I told you, no.

458
23:54.693 --> 23:56.533
Other older people usually don't like celebrities,

459
23:56.593 --> 23:59.203
but she seems a bit unique, right?

460
23:59.303 --> 24:01.773
You didn't know? Her husband.

461
24:01.833 --> 24:02.833
What?

462
24:04.603 --> 24:08.973
I mean, Mu I's grandfather was a very ordinary guy.

463
24:09.073 --> 24:13.013
He worked at some small company. But after marrying her,

464
24:13.083 --> 24:14.883
with all her scandals and rumors,

465
24:14.953 --> 24:17.083
and her being away for days on out-of-town shoots,

466
24:17.153 --> 24:20.193
he suffered from severe depression...

467
24:20.253 --> 24:21.393
and took his own...

468
24:22.393 --> 24:23.623
Really?

469
24:24.093 --> 24:25.563
Keep your voice down.

470
24:25.623 --> 24:26.623
Just plate the food.

471
24:26.833 --> 24:28.563
("Tak Mu I Trashes Conscience, Is He a Controversy Maker?")

472
24:36.603 --> 24:38.203
You remember, right?

473
24:38.703 --> 24:40.173
How Volume Two ended.

474
24:41.413 --> 24:42.473
Because of the bear bile extraction,

475
24:42.543 --> 24:45.143
the mother bear who suffered her whole life in a cage died,

476
24:48.683 --> 24:49.913
Yes.

477
24:49.983 --> 24:51.483
And Moon Bear, who was rescued alone,

478
24:51.553 --> 24:54.123
grew up healthy with the love of the zoo family,

479
24:54.193 --> 24:55.953
and the night before returning to the wild,

480
24:56.023 --> 24:58.023
it ends right there.

481
24:58.093 --> 24:59.163
I think it did.

482
25:00.593 --> 25:01.863
So,

483
25:02.633 --> 25:05.403
I need to see it with my own eyes that the released Moon Bear...

484
25:05.463 --> 25:09.303
is doing well for this long nightmare to end.

485
25:10.543 --> 25:11.543
So, then...

486
25:11.603 --> 25:14.073
do we go to that rooftop woman and take it by force?

487
25:14.173 --> 25:16.243
Or should we steal it?

488
25:16.343 --> 25:17.583
Are we robbers?

489
25:19.783 --> 25:22.583
The publisher. Let us go to the publisher.

490
25:22.653 --> 25:24.322
- Hi. - Oh, you are here?

491
25:24.323 --> 25:26.053
- Yes, hi. - Min Ye.

492
25:26.123 --> 25:27.653
Your waiting room is over there.

493
25:29.753 --> 25:31.623
I thought your waiting room was the same as mine.

494
25:32.923 --> 25:34.493
It has been a while, Mu I.

495
25:34.563 --> 25:36.193
Yes, have you been well?

496
25:36.263 --> 25:38.333
Of course I have.

497
25:38.403 --> 25:42.873
But it seems like you have not been doing so well lately.

498
25:42.933 --> 25:46.543
This advertiser is something else. It should have just been you and me.

499
25:46.603 --> 25:48.013
Why did they have to include her?

500
25:48.073 --> 25:51.613
The concept is "I will never yield." Not the man, not the coffee.

501
25:52.643 --> 25:54.483
Why did you do that with the lunchbox?

502
25:54.553 --> 25:56.683
If you were to throw it away, should have done it out of sight.

503
25:57.323 --> 25:58.923
And as for the movie...

504
25:59.753 --> 26:00.753
How is it doing?

505
26:02.623 --> 26:03.693
Never mind.

506
26:03.763 --> 26:06.293
Come to think of it, there are actors who work for movies...

507
26:06.363 --> 26:07.963
and actors who work for TV.

508
26:09.093 --> 26:12.133
Right. And you seem to work for YouTube.

509
26:13.403 --> 26:15.873
- What? - The drama you finished recently...

510
26:15.933 --> 26:17.403
did not get a single article written about it,

511
26:17.473 --> 26:19.673
but your vlog is making a huge fuss.

512
26:21.173 --> 26:22.343
It is so strange.

513
26:22.413 --> 26:24.583
Usually, if people are curious about what someone eats, wears,

514
26:24.643 --> 26:26.743
carries, or puts on,

515
26:26.813 --> 26:28.953
they are also curious about their actual job.

516
26:30.113 --> 26:31.423
Hey.

517
26:31.523 --> 26:33.653
At least I am starting a new project right away.

518
26:33.723 --> 26:36.493
Right, and for that project,

519
26:36.553 --> 26:39.823
- thank me for getting it. - Why would I?

520
26:39.893 --> 26:41.533
I turned that one down.

521
26:41.993 --> 26:44.303
If you want to keep picking up my leftovers,

522
26:46.733 --> 26:49.173
You should show some deep gratitude...

523
26:50.943 --> 26:52.243
in a not-so-boring way.

524
26:54.543 --> 26:55.573
You...

525
26:55.643 --> 26:57.743
I am going to check, and if you are lying, you are dead.

526
26:57.813 --> 26:58.813
Okay.

527
27:01.553 --> 27:03.083
Goodbye.

528
27:04.583 --> 27:06.423
Ju Da Hong wins by knockout.

529
27:07.693 --> 27:09.323
You are very reliable.

530
27:09.753 --> 27:11.623
If someone scratches my guy, I claw them.

531
27:14.093 --> 27:15.133
Meow.

532
27:17.533 --> 27:18.563
I am sorry.

533
27:18.633 --> 27:21.573
All the senior staff happen to be on a business trip overseas.

534
27:21.633 --> 27:24.573
It is fine. Did you find anything out?

535
27:24.603 --> 27:27.473
Right. The book was not officially published.

536
27:27.543 --> 27:30.113
They only printed a few copies as proofreading drafts.

537
27:30.173 --> 27:33.543
Like the paper, illustrations, and things like that as a draft.

538
27:34.213 --> 27:36.453
Even then, only a few people involved...

539
27:36.513 --> 27:38.353
and the author received copies.

540
27:40.353 --> 27:42.053
Would the publisher not have one?

541
27:42.123 --> 27:43.123
No.

542
27:43.193 --> 27:45.193
I looked for it, but we do not have it.

543
27:45.723 --> 27:47.733
When our publishing company moved,

544
27:47.863 --> 27:49.833
we probably threw them away.

545
27:59.503 --> 28:02.173
How on earth does Gong Yu Il have a book like that?

546
28:03.243 --> 28:04.813
Was she affiliated with the publisher?

547
28:04.883 --> 28:07.213
No, she is too young for that.

548
28:07.283 --> 28:08.753
Mr. Tak.

549
28:08.813 --> 28:09.813
- Yes. - The scene...

550
28:09.883 --> 28:12.123
we shot here last time, where you were eating ice cream...

551
28:12.183 --> 28:13.953
They said you have to reshoot it.

552
28:14.023 --> 28:16.923
- Why? - Min's acting was lacking,

553
28:16.993 --> 28:18.663
so his agency wants to reshoot it.

554
28:18.723 --> 28:21.233
- I see. - I am sorry. It is because of me.

555
28:21.293 --> 28:22.633
No, it is fine.

556
28:23.733 --> 28:25.233
- Si Eun. My clothes from yesterday. - Yes.

557
28:25.303 --> 28:26.303
Oh, okay.

558
28:28.503 --> 28:29.773
It is fine.

559
28:33.303 --> 28:34.913
You don't have the clothes?

560
28:34.973 --> 28:37.143
I clearly told them that we might have to reshoot...

561
28:37.213 --> 28:38.783
and to keep them ready.

562
28:38.843 --> 28:42.783
Oh, that shirt just disappeared without a trace.

563
28:43.183 --> 28:45.253
Gosh, what should we do?

564
28:45.323 --> 28:48.393
It is a continuity issue, so we cannot even change the outfit.

565
28:48.453 --> 28:51.863
Min's CEO begged me so much.

566
28:51.923 --> 28:55.063
And Min said he practiced his acting all night.

567
28:56.933 --> 28:58.803
Could we reshoot it tomorrow?

568
28:58.863 --> 29:00.333
I will try to find something similar.

569
29:00.403 --> 29:02.433
Well, it cannot be helped.

570
29:02.533 --> 29:06.143
I will explain it well to the director.

571
29:06.203 --> 29:07.973
- I am sorry. - It is fine.

572
29:09.573 --> 29:10.583
I am sorry!

573
29:12.583 --> 29:13.583
It is fine.

574
29:22.953 --> 29:23.963
Are you not leaving?

575
29:25.893 --> 29:27.063
I am going to sleep here tonight.

576
29:29.533 --> 29:31.203
Since you helped me with the script reading,

577
29:31.263 --> 29:32.663
I should repay you.

578
29:32.703 --> 29:35.133
Leaving now would be repaying me.

579
29:36.333 --> 29:39.242
No, Yeong Su said you cannot sleep at all...

580
29:39.243 --> 29:41.243
and asked me to sleep here with you.

581
29:44.043 --> 29:46.543
He still does not know me at all.

582
29:47.853 --> 29:49.083
Anyway,

583
29:49.153 --> 29:52.123
I have prepared everything to help you overcome your insomnia.

584
29:56.053 --> 29:58.163
But do you have any comfortable clothes I could wear?

585
29:59.293 --> 30:00.993
Next.

586
30:01.063 --> 30:04.833
Calcium and magnesium in a 2-to-1 ratio.

587
30:07.333 --> 30:10.173
And three one-gram pills of melatonin.

588
30:11.943 --> 30:12.943
Here, take them.

589
30:14.943 --> 30:18.513
- I take all of these at once? - Oh, of course.

590
30:18.613 --> 30:20.083
I take them like this every night before bed.

591
30:25.223 --> 30:27.893
Now, the first one is the cow head pose.

592
30:27.953 --> 30:30.393
- Like this? - Yes, cross your legs.

593
30:30.453 --> 30:33.263
Go down just like this, in this way.

594
30:33.323 --> 30:35.063
Hey, I cannot go down.

595
30:35.733 --> 30:37.533
No, you have to go down further.

596
30:37.563 --> 30:38.563
Here.

597
30:39.333 --> 30:43.633
- Hey, Min! - You have to endure it.

598
30:43.703 --> 30:46.373
- Stop! - Now, the next one is the cat pose.

599
30:47.473 --> 30:48.743
Hurry up and try it.

600
30:48.813 --> 30:51.183
- Stretch more. - Forward...

601
30:51.243 --> 30:53.313
- You bent your upper body too much. - Oh, well...

602
30:53.383 --> 30:55.813
- Hey! - That's it. A good stretch, right?

603
30:55.883 --> 30:58.583
What stretch? Goodness.

604
30:58.653 --> 31:01.753
Now, the last one is called the happy baby pose.

605
31:01.823 --> 31:03.453
Lie down.

606
31:03.523 --> 31:07.333
- Oh, this is a bit much, Min. - But this works instantly, really.

607
31:07.393 --> 31:09.033
- Right here... - Go easy.

608
31:09.093 --> 31:10.603
- Hey! - Bear with it.

609
31:10.663 --> 31:14.303
No. Hey!

610
31:18.173 --> 31:20.743
Now, breathe in through your nose.

611
31:23.913 --> 31:24.913
Hold it.

612
31:26.743 --> 31:29.883
And slowly exhale through your mouth.

613
31:32.953 --> 31:35.123
If you repeat this process four times,

614
31:35.193 --> 31:36.793
you will soon fall asleep.

615
31:39.663 --> 31:41.663
Like this is going to make me fall asleep?

616
31:50.203 --> 31:51.273
It does help.

617
31:57.513 --> 31:58.513
(Writer Kkongkkong's Practice Notebook)

618
31:58.583 --> 32:01.013
(Writer Kkongkkong, Congratulations on the Grand Prize.)

619
32:04.053 --> 32:08.823
(Award Ceremony for Recommended Youth Books)

620
32:17.193 --> 32:19.003
The connection cannot be made. After the beep...

621
32:19.063 --> 32:20.603
What do we do if the Grand Prize winner does not show?

622
32:26.543 --> 32:28.013
(Write a post)

623
32:32.283 --> 32:37.423
(I can't find it!)

624
32:53.833 --> 32:56.703
We tried to find something as similar to this as possible.

625
32:56.773 --> 32:58.203
No, look.

626
32:58.703 --> 33:00.843
The buttons are different, the collar shape is different.

627
33:00.913 --> 33:03.513
And the most important thing, these stripes.

628
33:03.573 --> 33:05.713
The thickness of these stripes is different.

629
33:07.243 --> 33:09.613
Gosh, what do we do now?

630
33:10.183 --> 33:11.623
Are we supposed to reshoot the connecting scenes too?

631
33:12.853 --> 33:14.593
I found it!

632
33:14.653 --> 33:15.653
- What? - Really?

633
33:15.723 --> 33:17.723
- I found it. - Great job.

634
33:17.793 --> 33:19.493
I found it.

635
33:19.563 --> 33:21.593
- I found it. - Good job.

636
33:23.033 --> 33:26.063
I mean, it definitely was not here just a minute ago.

637
33:26.133 --> 33:28.073
But after I helped him get dressed and came out,

638
33:28.133 --> 33:30.433
it was hanging right here as if to show off.

639
33:30.503 --> 33:32.973
- That is really strange. - Yes.

640
33:34.513 --> 33:36.343
It happens.

641
33:36.443 --> 33:37.443
What?

642
33:39.413 --> 33:41.283
Did you spray perfume by any chance?

643
33:41.313 --> 33:42.453
No.

644
33:42.483 --> 33:45.723
Why would I spray perfume on sponsored clothes? It would stain.

645
33:45.783 --> 33:46.783
Smell this.

646
33:47.923 --> 33:48.953
What?

647
33:49.623 --> 33:50.623
What is this?

648
33:50.693 --> 33:52.323
- You are right. - What?

649
33:54.363 --> 33:55.793
It smells expensive.

650
33:55.863 --> 33:57.193
- It is expensive? - Yes.

651
33:58.603 --> 33:59.603
What is it?

652
34:00.703 --> 34:02.973
Cut. Okay.

653
34:03.033 --> 34:06.903
- Great work, everyone. - Great work.

654
34:08.513 --> 34:11.783
Man, these numbers are not going up at all.

655
34:13.283 --> 34:15.383
The "Free Egg" score keeps dropping too.

656
34:16.013 --> 34:20.083
We cannot even make the top five on Lucky Cinema's "Want to See."

657
34:20.153 --> 34:21.453
We are stuck in sixth place.

658
34:22.993 --> 34:25.993
We are even ranked lower than movies that have already been released.

659
34:29.533 --> 34:31.533
What? "Heartsping of Love" rewatch.

660
34:31.903 --> 34:32.933
This is in fifth place.

661
34:33.963 --> 34:37.943
You cannot beat Heartsping!

662
34:38.003 --> 34:39.703
Until the next series comes out,

663
34:39.773 --> 34:41.373
the kids watch it over and over again.

664
34:41.413 --> 34:43.673
They watch it at home, and if it is in theaters, they watch it again.

665
34:43.743 --> 34:45.343
They keep rewatching it just like you do with Moon Bear,

666
34:45.413 --> 34:46.783
so how can you win?

667
34:46.843 --> 34:49.683
I want to see Moon Bear too.

668
34:51.623 --> 34:53.253
- Hey. - What?

669
34:53.383 --> 34:54.753
The premiere is one thing,

670
34:54.823 --> 34:56.623
but once it is released, everyone will be paying to see it.

671
34:56.693 --> 34:57.693
Yes.

672
34:57.763 --> 34:59.393
What if they say it was a waste of money?

673
34:59.763 --> 35:01.393
And when we go around for the stage greetings,

674
35:01.463 --> 35:02.893
what if only two or three people are sitting there?

675
35:02.963 --> 35:04.463
Oh, come on, that would never happen.

676
35:04.533 --> 35:05.533
Just hurry up and go.

677
35:07.033 --> 35:08.333
I am supposed to be your manager,

678
35:08.403 --> 35:10.673
but I am sorry there is nothing I can do for you.

679
35:12.803 --> 35:14.003
Wait a minute.

680
35:14.073 --> 35:16.873
- What? - That smell. It's that perfume.

681
35:17.513 --> 35:19.343
What perfume smell? Let's go now.

682
35:19.413 --> 35:21.783
No, it is the same smell from that shirt.

683
35:21.853 --> 35:24.083
What smell? Come on, let's go.

684
35:59.523 --> 36:02.293
(I apologize for bothering you.)

685
36:05.393 --> 36:06.793
Gosh.

686
36:06.863 --> 36:09.663
Is Tak Mu I making you do things like this now?

687
36:09.793 --> 36:11.263
A sketchbook? How old-fashioned.

688
36:12.403 --> 36:14.033
Honestly, at this point,

689
36:14.103 --> 36:16.703
Tak Mu I is the stalker, not me, right?

690
36:19.403 --> 36:21.972
I thought only job seekers had it hard,

691
36:21.973 --> 36:24.043
but making a living is tough for managers too.

692
36:25.143 --> 36:28.113
I mean, if he wants it so badly, he should come himself.

693
36:28.213 --> 36:30.083
Why make an innocent person suffer?

694
36:30.613 --> 36:32.523
This is a power trip. What else would you call it?

695
36:34.223 --> 36:35.393
What?

696
36:36.193 --> 36:37.793
Oh, my.

697
36:37.893 --> 36:39.163
Are you crying?

698
36:40.463 --> 36:42.433
Oh, well, it is about time you let it out.

699
36:42.493 --> 36:45.503
Here, at least take this off and have a good cry.

700
36:45.603 --> 36:48.073
Oh, wait, would that be more embarrassing?

701
36:48.103 --> 36:50.303
Just cry, let it out.

702
36:57.913 --> 36:59.443
Gosh, the dust...

703
37:00.783 --> 37:02.183
I have a bit of a dust allergy.

704
37:09.093 --> 37:10.453
So, why...

705
37:10.523 --> 37:13.523
would someone with allergies wear something like this?

706
37:13.593 --> 37:14.693
Oh, well...

707
37:15.133 --> 37:18.103
To show my sincerity about wanting to meet Moon Bear.

708
37:18.503 --> 37:21.073
- If it is about that... - Oh, no.

709
37:21.403 --> 37:23.803
I came today to sincerely apologize.

710
37:25.503 --> 37:27.673
You kept saying you were not, but I treated you like a stalker,

711
37:27.743 --> 37:29.843
and I am sorry for being rude.

712
37:31.283 --> 37:33.913
You must have felt offended, and I apologize.

713
37:34.753 --> 37:36.253
Well, in any case,

714
37:36.753 --> 37:39.783
you did save me, and with that moth too.

715
37:40.583 --> 37:43.523
I made you go through things you did not have to,

716
37:43.623 --> 37:45.623
so I am sorry too.

717
37:46.863 --> 37:49.393
So, do you accept my apology?

718
37:51.203 --> 37:52.503
I guess.

719
37:53.203 --> 37:55.603
But are you okay?

720
37:57.573 --> 37:58.943
About what?

721
37:59.003 --> 38:02.843
Oh, last time, you said you really needed that book.

722
38:03.943 --> 38:05.243
Is something going on?

723
38:07.083 --> 38:10.583
Oh, I do not really want to talk about this, but...

724
38:11.823 --> 38:13.883
When I was going through a really hard time,

725
38:13.953 --> 38:15.493
I once went on a trip without a plan.

726
38:16.323 --> 38:19.063
At that time, my sister said she really wanted me to read it,

727
38:19.123 --> 38:20.292
so she gave me "Byeol I and Moon Bear,"

728
38:20.293 --> 38:21.463
and that was my first time reading.

729
38:23.193 --> 38:26.403
Oh, your sister did that.

730
38:27.233 --> 38:28.503
Anyway,

731
38:28.903 --> 38:31.203
I found a lot of comfort in reading that book,

732
38:33.173 --> 38:34.913
and I have been in a similar situation lately.

733
38:36.243 --> 38:38.113
Maybe it is because I have read it so much.

734
38:38.213 --> 38:39.813
Volumes 1 and 2 are not enough to fix it.

735
38:47.353 --> 38:48.353
What?

736
38:50.623 --> 38:52.093
What? This smell...

737
38:52.163 --> 38:54.063
What is this smell? Wait...

738
38:54.123 --> 38:56.333
- What fragrance is that? - What?

739
38:58.933 --> 39:01.503
Oh, is it my hand cream?

740
39:04.003 --> 39:07.373
Oh, this is hair perfume.

741
39:07.843 --> 39:10.273
I used it because I did not wash my hair.

742
39:10.343 --> 39:12.213
But why?

743
39:12.283 --> 39:14.283
No, it is just that it smells exactly like that stalker...

744
39:14.343 --> 39:15.353
What?

745
39:16.413 --> 39:17.883
Oh, seriously.

746
39:18.153 --> 39:19.323
Hey.

747
39:20.053 --> 39:21.822
I was going to let it go because I felt bad for you.

748
39:21.823 --> 39:23.893
What? I smell like a stalker?

749
39:23.953 --> 39:26.192
- Oh, no, that is not what I meant. - Hey.

750
39:26.193 --> 39:28.263
Is having a handsome face everything?

751
39:28.333 --> 39:31.203
You are a hopeless narcissist who thinks everyone is into you.

752
39:31.263 --> 39:32.463
Could you just leave?

753
39:32.533 --> 39:34.803
Oh, you should really listen to me...

754
39:34.873 --> 39:36.403
Are you not leaving?

755
39:37.433 --> 39:38.973
- I will shoot, okay? - No.

756
39:39.043 --> 39:40.243
- Go. - You should really listen to me...

757
39:40.303 --> 39:42.043
- Go! - No, seriously.

758
39:45.813 --> 39:46.913
Gosh, seriously.

759
39:47.243 --> 39:48.283
(I apologize for bothering you.)

760
39:49.213 --> 39:50.213
Goodness.

761
39:55.593 --> 39:57.963
(I am sorry for misunderstanding.)

762
39:58.023 --> 39:59.593
(I am also sorry for being annoying.)

763
39:59.663 --> 40:03.163
(I was just so curious about what happened to Byeol I and Moon Bear.)

764
40:04.533 --> 40:06.763
Was I too harsh on a sick person?

765
40:10.873 --> 40:15.673
(Will you accept my apology?)

766
40:17.513 --> 40:21.313
Patient Choi Ji Hyeok. Where does it hurt?

767
40:21.413 --> 40:23.953
Oh, my ears hurt.

768
40:24.413 --> 40:26.083
Why do your ears hurt?

769
40:26.683 --> 40:28.993
Oh, because of my mom's nagging.

770
40:30.093 --> 40:31.093
I see.

771
40:32.863 --> 40:35.733
Well, I will get your medicine ready right away.

772
40:35.793 --> 40:36.793
Okay.

773
40:41.873 --> 40:43.503
Here is your medicine.

774
40:43.573 --> 40:46.173
- Get well soon. - Thank you.

775
40:55.313 --> 40:56.483
Next patient?

776
40:57.483 --> 40:58.953
(Poa Kids Cafe, The Kitchen)

777
40:59.023 --> 41:00.283
(Clockwork Owl Workshop, Hana Neighborhood Park)

778
41:08.633 --> 41:09.933
May I sit next to you?

779
41:29.753 --> 41:31.083
You must be a chef.

780
41:32.083 --> 41:33.123
I am a pharmacist.

781
41:34.423 --> 41:36.123
Oh, yes.

782
41:36.523 --> 41:38.163
What kind of food do you make?

783
41:40.063 --> 41:44.163
Well, I make pasta and steaks.

784
41:46.733 --> 41:47.933
The kids are so cute, right?

785
41:49.803 --> 41:52.173
Kids are cute, of course.

786
41:53.073 --> 41:55.813
The day before yesterday, I asked a kid,

787
41:56.143 --> 42:00.713
"Where does it hurt?" and he rubbed his chest...

788
42:00.783 --> 42:03.183
and said, "It hurts here."

789
42:03.283 --> 42:06.183
He said he got rejected after asking a girl in his class out.

790
42:11.193 --> 42:12.193
That is cute.

791
42:13.693 --> 42:16.993
Oh, it would be great if there was a medicine for that.

792
42:17.933 --> 42:19.933
People who failed to get a job,

793
42:20.433 --> 42:22.473
people who got their hearts broken,

794
42:22.533 --> 42:24.703
people who are upset because things are not working out.

795
42:25.143 --> 42:28.013
If those people could just swallow one pill,

796
42:28.113 --> 42:29.973
their pain would be swallowed up too.

797
42:31.443 --> 42:33.383
If I could make a medicine like that,

798
42:33.443 --> 42:35.283
I would study really hard...

799
42:35.353 --> 42:37.683
and it would be nice to become a pharmacist.

800
42:37.753 --> 42:39.953
I have thoughts like that.

801
42:41.183 --> 42:42.193
Goodness.

802
42:49.463 --> 42:50.933
Oh, I am sorry.

803
42:50.993 --> 42:53.863
I talked too much to someone I just met, right?

804
42:53.963 --> 42:56.473
No, it is not because of that.

805
42:59.143 --> 43:01.413
That is mine.

806
43:02.843 --> 43:05.343
Excuse me? Oh, my goodness.

807
43:05.783 --> 43:08.483
Oh, my, I am sorry. What should I do about this?

808
43:08.553 --> 43:10.513
I already put my mouth on it.

809
43:17.523 --> 43:18.563
You put your room up for rent?

810
43:19.793 --> 43:21.733
Do you know what the best part about this place is?

811
43:22.863 --> 43:24.863
Well, the best part?

812
43:26.703 --> 43:28.033
The view?

813
43:28.273 --> 43:31.803
- The sunset? - No, the address.

814
43:32.503 --> 43:34.003
The address?

815
43:34.103 --> 43:35.743
When I lived in a semi-basement,

816
43:35.813 --> 43:39.043
I hated that I always had to write "basement" in front of it.

817
43:39.083 --> 43:40.683
But if I did not write it,

818
43:40.783 --> 43:43.183
all my packages and mail would go to the first floor.

819
43:44.823 --> 43:48.153
But here, you cannot tell just by looking at the address.

820
43:49.923 --> 43:51.253
Cut, okay.

821
43:51.693 --> 43:53.423
- Let us take a short break. - Yes.

822
43:53.493 --> 43:54.933
We are taking a break.

823
44:02.473 --> 44:04.673
Darn. It's Mu I again.

824
44:05.773 --> 44:06.943
Hi, there.

825
44:08.543 --> 44:10.513
Oh, hi.

826
44:10.643 --> 44:13.313
Producer Yeon Ju said you are a job seeker.

827
44:13.883 --> 44:15.813
You know I am playing a job seeker in this drama too, right?

828
44:16.883 --> 44:18.953
Oh, yes, I heard.

829
44:19.023 --> 44:21.893
I am having a hard time getting a feel for it.

830
44:21.953 --> 44:25.193
Should I call it an interview? Or research?

831
44:25.823 --> 44:28.793
Oh, right, consulting. Could I ask you for some advice?

832
44:36.773 --> 44:38.703
Are you not scared living in a place like this?

833
44:41.103 --> 44:42.543
I am scared.

834
44:42.613 --> 44:45.283
That is why I keep my doors locked and double-locked.

835
44:49.283 --> 44:51.213
Oh, what is it like living as a job seeker?

836
44:53.153 --> 44:54.993
Well, let me see.

837
44:56.293 --> 44:57.523
How should I put it?

838
44:59.423 --> 45:01.123
It feels like I am floating.

839
45:04.233 --> 45:06.103
Oh, just like that,

840
45:07.463 --> 45:11.803
I am definitely growing, and I am living well day by day,

841
45:12.173 --> 45:14.673
but it feels like I cannot put my roots down in the ground.

842
45:16.243 --> 45:17.273
Are you not anxious?

843
45:19.583 --> 45:20.583
No.

844
45:21.713 --> 45:23.813
Even on nights when nothing happens,

845
45:24.953 --> 45:26.453
the towels dry,

846
45:26.883 --> 45:28.253
the plants grow,

847
45:28.323 --> 45:30.653
and packages just arrive in front of the house.

848
45:31.223 --> 45:34.263
I believe something is happening during my nights too.

849
45:34.833 --> 45:36.193
I do not doubt it.

850
45:36.263 --> 45:39.063
If I do not believe in myself, who will?

851
45:39.133 --> 45:43.033
Oh, that is so cool, Yu Il. I can call you Yu Il, right?

852
45:43.703 --> 45:45.173
Yes.

853
45:45.243 --> 45:46.243
You are cool.

854
45:52.513 --> 45:53.513
Hold on a second.

855
46:01.923 --> 46:03.123
What are you doing here?

856
46:04.253 --> 46:06.463
Oh, I was just wondering what all this was.

857
46:07.923 --> 46:10.633
What do you mean? They are cacti.

858
46:11.133 --> 46:12.463
Do you seriously not know what a cactus is?

859
46:14.403 --> 46:17.333
Oh, so these are all cacti. I see.

860
46:18.973 --> 46:21.643
Da Hong, when you live alone,

861
46:22.143 --> 46:24.513
you have to be especially careful of people like him.

862
46:24.983 --> 46:27.443
Mu I, were you eavesdropping?

863
46:27.483 --> 46:29.183
Were you curious about what I was doing?

864
46:29.253 --> 46:33.523
- No, it is not like that... - Come on, I know it is.

865
46:33.583 --> 46:36.293
You were so curious because I was out of sight.

866
46:36.723 --> 46:37.993
Seriously!

867
46:40.363 --> 46:42.663
So they have that kind of relationship.

868
46:46.103 --> 46:49.173
By the way, Yu Il, you must really like Ryu Min.

869
46:49.633 --> 46:51.073
Oh, right.

870
46:51.133 --> 46:52.843
Thank you for the tea.

871
46:52.943 --> 46:54.302
- Da Hong, get ready. - Okay.

872
46:54.303 --> 46:55.673
Thank you, Yu Il. See you later.

873
46:57.673 --> 46:59.913
- Hello. - Hello.

874
47:00.313 --> 47:02.553
You must be a fan of Ryu Min.

875
47:03.613 --> 47:05.923
Gosh, that is impressive for a job seeker.

876
47:06.783 --> 47:08.083
Do your parents not mind?

877
47:08.593 --> 47:10.493
Oh, parents usually do not like this kind of thing.

878
47:10.693 --> 47:11.723
- Director. - Yes.

879
47:11.793 --> 47:14.323
- I brought this for you to drink. - Oh, my, how thoughtful.

880
47:14.933 --> 47:17.263
Your shoulders are really tense, Director.

881
47:17.333 --> 47:19.603
- Let me massage them for you. - What? Okay.

882
47:20.863 --> 47:22.003
That feels good.

883
47:22.603 --> 47:24.833
- They are so tense. - Gosh.

884
47:24.903 --> 47:26.103
Stop it.

885
47:26.303 --> 47:27.803
- Gosh! - It feels refreshing, right?

886
47:28.213 --> 47:31.743
Gosh, stop. I said, stop!

887
47:33.413 --> 47:35.183
I told you to stop!

888
47:35.253 --> 47:37.683
Hurry up and get ready. Gosh, it hurts.

889
47:37.983 --> 47:39.583
Well, they were just really tense.

890
47:43.753 --> 47:46.963
That was partly to apologize for eavesdropping earlier...

891
47:47.023 --> 47:48.023
and partly revenge on your behalf.

892
47:49.963 --> 47:52.103
I never asked you to get revenge for me.

893
47:52.163 --> 47:55.033
No matter what you do, I cannot give you the book.

894
47:57.073 --> 47:58.273
Then sell it to me.

895
48:00.473 --> 48:01.873
How much will you give me?

896
48:02.343 --> 48:04.343
Oh, you would know if you had eavesdropped earlier.

897
48:04.443 --> 48:06.883
I am a job seeker, so I am struggling a lot.

898
48:07.443 --> 48:09.553
About 100,000 dollars?

899
48:09.613 --> 48:10.753
I will sell it if you give me that.

900
48:13.253 --> 48:14.383
You are a total thief.

901
48:17.793 --> 48:20.323
Gosh. First a stalker, and now...

902
48:20.823 --> 48:21.893
a thief?

903
48:23.893 --> 48:26.563
Will you get out before I report you for trespassing?

904
48:27.603 --> 48:28.933
That is not what I meant.

905
48:29.003 --> 48:30.273
Get out!

906
48:33.543 --> 48:34.543
Seriously.

907
48:34.603 --> 48:35.973
(Flowers bloom on the rooftop too.)

908
48:46.383 --> 48:50.453
Are you getting even skinnier? Please get some sleep today.

909
48:50.523 --> 48:52.193
You are going to end up in serious trouble at this rate.

910
48:53.963 --> 48:57.433
Moon Bear, where are you?

911
48:57.493 --> 49:00.363
If you can hear me, please answer.

912
49:03.073 --> 49:05.843
I think you need help from a medical professional.

913
49:05.903 --> 49:07.773
I wonder if Jae Gyu is still at the hospital.

914
49:07.843 --> 49:11.043
Forget it. Jae Gyu is completely unsympathetic.

915
49:11.113 --> 49:12.983
He will prescribe sleeping pills instead of empathizing.

916
49:18.683 --> 49:19.683
What is this?

917
49:21.383 --> 49:22.953
What is that now?

918
49:23.023 --> 49:25.023
A YouTube reunion frequency.

919
49:25.093 --> 49:26.763
Min said it was good.

920
49:26.823 --> 49:29.633
It is the desire of our generation...

921
49:29.693 --> 49:31.393
to somehow reconnect with our exes, I guess?

922
49:33.603 --> 49:35.373
If I keep listening to it,

923
49:35.433 --> 49:38.543
my broken connection with Moon Bear might be restored.

924
49:38.603 --> 49:40.273
Unbelievable.

925
49:40.343 --> 49:45.243
Okay, if you are into shamanism, let's just go there instead.

926
49:47.543 --> 49:48.553
Go where?

927
49:53.183 --> 49:55.093
Why do you have this stuff in your house?

928
49:55.153 --> 49:56.823
Is it not distracting?

929
49:57.123 --> 49:58.963
What are you curious about?

930
50:00.263 --> 50:02.733
So what does she do again?

931
50:02.793 --> 50:06.503
Not "she." I am Tarot Master Rosa.

932
50:07.203 --> 50:08.633
Master?

933
50:08.703 --> 50:10.033
You cannot even play Go-Stop.

934
50:10.103 --> 50:12.973
Darn it. I am not doing this. Take him away.

935
50:13.043 --> 50:14.543
All right.

936
50:14.603 --> 50:15.843
You, Da Hong...

937
50:17.543 --> 50:21.083
- Rosa. - You saw Rosa catch Min Ye, right?

938
50:21.143 --> 50:23.413
She is really good at this. She is spot on.

939
50:23.483 --> 50:26.223
What does that have to do with this?

940
50:27.653 --> 50:28.653
Rosa?

941
50:32.763 --> 50:36.133
Think about what you want to know, and pick a card.

942
50:43.603 --> 50:46.003
The Devil card represents strong desire,

943
50:46.073 --> 50:48.343
obsession, and lingering attachment.

944
50:49.043 --> 50:51.573
You must want something very badly.

945
50:52.113 --> 50:56.113
To the other person, you might seem like a devil.

946
51:01.023 --> 51:02.023
Well...

947
51:03.323 --> 51:05.563
Will I be able to find what I'm looking for?

948
51:05.623 --> 51:06.793
Pick one more card.

949
51:18.673 --> 51:19.943
Death.

950
51:20.003 --> 51:22.243
That's right, the writer is dead, right?

951
51:22.313 --> 51:26.113
- Or does he die? - No.

952
51:26.513 --> 51:29.253
The world of tarot is not that simple.

953
51:29.313 --> 51:33.453
An ending can also mean a new beginning.

954
51:35.353 --> 51:37.593
So, will I find it or not?

955
51:38.993 --> 51:43.733
The current phase will end, and you will face a new phase.

956
51:46.103 --> 51:47.903
It means you'll find it.

957
51:47.963 --> 51:49.273
Where is it? Where do I need to go?

958
52:04.553 --> 52:06.923
What does this card mean?

959
52:10.023 --> 52:11.493
Well, that is...

960
52:11.553 --> 52:13.963
What is this handwriting?

961
52:15.493 --> 52:16.493
Right.

962
52:17.693 --> 52:21.033
Does it mean "unique" in Italian?

963
52:21.363 --> 52:23.973
It meant something like that.

964
52:26.603 --> 52:27.843
What?

965
52:27.903 --> 52:30.173
What? Only one?

966
52:44.723 --> 52:45.723
Yes.

967
52:47.993 --> 52:50.733
I found it. It was on the desk.

968
52:51.163 --> 52:55.403
Oh, what a relief. Could you bring it to the set?

969
52:55.473 --> 52:58.003
It has the schedule and everything.

970
52:58.073 --> 53:01.343
- I'm sorry, Yu Il. - Oh, don't be sorry.

971
53:01.403 --> 53:02.413
Where should I go?

972
53:03.413 --> 53:05.073
("Rooftop Romance")

973
53:05.143 --> 53:06.913
(Way to go, Tak Mu I!)

974
53:06.983 --> 53:09.783
(Supporting Actor Tak Mu I and the "Rooftop Romance" team)

975
53:13.383 --> 53:15.123
- Thanks for the drink. - Enjoy.

976
53:15.183 --> 53:16.523
Enjoy.

977
53:16.653 --> 53:17.993
You regret doing a romance with Da Hong, right?

978
53:19.823 --> 53:21.163
I'll have a latte, please.

979
53:21.493 --> 53:25.903
Why? I like it. I get to hug and kiss him.

980
53:25.963 --> 53:28.673
I'm begging the writer because there's no deep kiss scene.

981
53:28.733 --> 53:31.173
Hey, there are a lot of people here.

982
53:31.233 --> 53:33.603
If you do not want to be on camera, just do it now.

983
53:34.803 --> 53:36.443
What do you want to drink?

984
53:36.513 --> 53:37.513
I'll have...

985
53:38.743 --> 53:42.913
- Hey. - Thanks, Yu Il. You saved my life.

986
53:42.983 --> 53:45.653
Here. Are you on a break right now?

987
53:45.753 --> 53:48.383
Yes, as you can see, a coffee truck arrived.

988
53:48.453 --> 53:49.453
Wait just a minute.

989
53:49.523 --> 53:50.822
I will get some stuff done...

990
53:50.823 --> 53:52.363
- and get us coffee. - Okay.

991
53:56.633 --> 53:57.763
What?

992
53:58.363 --> 53:59.933
The Tower. Only one.

993
54:01.063 --> 54:02.533
What are you talking about?

994
54:02.603 --> 54:04.433
She's the only way.

995
54:05.543 --> 54:07.403
(Supporting Actor Tak Mu I and the "Rooftop Romance" team)

996
54:09.273 --> 54:10.613
Who is that?

997
54:10.673 --> 54:13.043
Oh, she's the one who lives in the rooftop apartment...

998
54:13.113 --> 54:14.513
I live in on the show.

999
54:14.583 --> 54:15.713
She's a friend of the junior producer.

1000
54:18.413 --> 54:19.583
What brings you here?

1001
54:21.253 --> 54:23.153
Oh, I had some business to take care of.

1002
54:23.223 --> 54:26.363
Of course, that business does not involve you.

1003
54:26.523 --> 54:29.393
And could you please pretend not to know me if you see me?

1004
54:29.463 --> 54:31.093
You should stay away from your stalker.

1005
54:31.163 --> 54:33.633
If you keep being nice to me, I might get the wrong idea.

1006
54:37.033 --> 54:38.803
Have this. It is new.

1007
54:39.573 --> 54:41.943
Oh, I am fine. My friend is bringing me one.

1008
54:45.043 --> 54:46.043
Hey,

1009
54:46.113 --> 54:47.643
- Yes? - Thank you for the coffee.

1010
54:47.713 --> 54:48.713
Sure.

1011
54:49.553 --> 54:51.113
Oh, hello, Lim Su Kyung.

1012
54:53.023 --> 54:54.023
Oh, hi.

1013
54:55.853 --> 54:57.223
Lim Su Kyung?

1014
54:58.923 --> 55:00.663
This is Gong Yu Il.

1015
55:00.923 --> 55:02.863
Oh, I am sorry.

1016
55:04.233 --> 55:05.263
Oh, it is fine.

1017
55:06.603 --> 55:07.733
Darn it.

1018
55:07.803 --> 55:10.503
After leaving my room in that state,

1019
55:10.573 --> 55:12.373
I cannot exactly say I am not your fan now.

1020
55:13.903 --> 55:17.073
Would you like to have this? I just got it.

1021
55:17.173 --> 55:19.983
Oh, yes, thank you.

1022
55:20.443 --> 55:23.213
It will probably taste even better since you gave it to me.

1023
55:24.713 --> 55:27.623
Did you get the limited edition photocard this time?

1024
55:28.653 --> 55:30.293
Oh, the photocard?

1025
55:31.523 --> 55:32.523
Not yet.

1026
55:33.963 --> 55:35.593
Then I will bring it to you.

1027
55:36.133 --> 55:37.133
Just a moment.

1028
55:40.803 --> 55:44.333
But why would celebrity merchandise include poker cards?

1029
55:44.403 --> 55:46.003
It is not like they are encouraging gambling.

1030
55:47.543 --> 55:49.013
You do not know what a photocard is?

1031
55:50.113 --> 55:51.113
Photocard.

1032
55:53.743 --> 55:55.113
Oh, photocard!

1033
55:56.413 --> 55:57.413
Right.

1034
55:58.853 --> 56:01.323
A superfan who does not even know what a photocard is.

1035
56:01.383 --> 56:03.723
And you flat-out rejected what I offered,

1036
56:03.793 --> 56:05.663
but you accepted Min's right away.

1037
56:05.723 --> 56:07.693
It is clear you are not my fan.

1038
56:08.223 --> 56:10.133
You sure figured that out quickly.

1039
56:10.193 --> 56:12.703
If you have nothing else to say, you can leave now.

1040
56:13.163 --> 56:15.873
No, I have a ton of things to say.

1041
56:30.383 --> 56:31.883
(Way to go, Tak Mu I!)

1042
56:54.043 --> 56:55.203
("To You")

1043
56:55.273 --> 56:58.313
(Epilogue)

1044
57:11.493 --> 57:13.863
Mu I, take this with you.

1045
57:14.463 --> 57:15.993
I think it is a book you really need.

1046
57:17.293 --> 57:18.293
Really?

1047
57:23.573 --> 57:26.403
("Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 2, "Byeol I and Moon Bear" Volume 3)
